{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Org campaign board layout — where every zone sits on the polar map. Companion to org_regions.json (which owns what the zones ARE).",
    "updated": "2026-08-05",
    "src": "Planet, gate, station and belt positions copied verbatim from the Strata map layout (Mining repo, data/mining_data.json -> map_positions) — the distance-correct polar arrangement already used for routing. Satellite offsets are new and display-only.",
    "projection": "Polar. angle = degrees, 0 = north (12 o'clock), clockwise. Radius = ring x ringSpacing, where ringSpacing = canvasSize x ring_scale/100 / (maxRing + 0.5). Nodes with edge:true sit at canvasSize x edge_scale/100. Belts: belt_radius x ringSpacing (or ring x ringSpacing when given as ring). Matches Strata js/map.js toXY: x = cx + cos(a-90)*r, y = cy + sin(a-90)*r.",
    "satellites": "Zones with a parent render at the parent's XY plus a polar offset (moonAngle, moonDist x ringSpacing), same compass convention. The arrangement is cosmetic — real moons orbit constantly; only the parent relationship is meaningful. moonDist ladder follows each family's inner-to-outer order.",
    "zones": "Keys are org_regions.json zone ids — the two files join on them. landmarks are non-target flavor markers that keep the map honest and alive (Pyro's small stations, Nyx People Service stations). Nyx I-III are deliberately absent: map-only bodies, never destinations.",
    "gates": "Jump gates carry to: the system they lead to (null = not yet a destination). v1 renders them as landmarks; v2 promotes them to chokepoint zones."
  },

